  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Yusuf. You're verified.\n\nI've looked into order #6601. Spice Route has an open incident affecting orders placed between 5:00 and 7:00 PM tonight: their supplier recalled a sauce batch used in their curries. Your order was placed at 6:58 PM, so it's covered.\n\nWhen an incident like this covers an order, I can't refund or credit anything on it myself. Instead, I've sent your case to the incident team, including the chicken makhani you got instead of paneer makhani (reference **ESC-700**). They're contacting and compensating every affected order, and a specialist will get back to you within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll decide, but they have all the details.\n\nSince this involves a recalled sauce, I'd suggest not eating the curry from that order. **Has anyone eaten it or felt unwell?** If so, let me know right away so I can also flag it as a food-safety issue.\n\nWhat went wrong with your other order or orders tonight?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Nobody ate the chicken makhani, so everyone's fine, thank goodness. Good that it's been flagged.\n\nOk, so the other problems. I placed a second, smaller Spice Route order, #6602, a few minutes after the first one, just for extra naan. One of the two garlic naans was missing when it arrived.\n\nAlso, the third order from Lotus Garden, #6603, was missing the spring rolls.\n\nIs the refund for those going to my card? I'd really prefer that to credit on the app."
