  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm glad nobody ate the curry. Both refunds are going back to your Visa ending 4242, as you asked:\n\n- **Order #6602 (Spice Route), 1 missing garlic naan:** refunded **$4.00** (reference RF-4000). This order was placed at 7:02 PM, after the recall window closed, so I could handle it directly.\n- **Order #6603 (Lotus Garden), missing spring rolls:** refunded **$7.00** (reference RF-4001).\n\nThat's **$11.00** in total. It should reach your card in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nYou might also see two entries per order on your statement right now. One of them is a temporary hold from when you placed the order, and it's already been released. It will disappear on its own in 1\u20133 business days, and you're only charged once.\n\nOrder #6601 is still with the incident team (ESC-700), and they'll contact you within 24 hours.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with? I hope the rest of your evening goes well."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for sorting the naan and the spring rolls. $11 back on the Visa is good.\n\nQuick question though: you said the incident team will contact me within 24 hours about the chicken makhani. Will I still get refunded for that one, or do I have to do something else to make sure it happens?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You don't need to do anything else. Your case for order #6601 is filed with the incident team under reference **ESC-700**. It includes the paneer makhani that was swapped for chicken makhani and the fact that your order is covered by the sauce recall.\n\nI can't tell you what the incident team will decide or how much they'll give, because that's up to them. They're reaching out to every order affected by the recall, and a specialist will contact you within 24 hours. If you want to check on it before then, just mention ESC-700 when you contact support.\n\nSince this order is with the incident team, I can't add a refund or credit for it here. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Got it, thanks. So the naan and spring rolls are sorted, and #6601 is with the incident team under ESC-700. Nobody got sick, so that's the main thing.\n\nI think that's everything for now. Appreciate the help tonight."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, that's all correct:\n\n- **#6602 (garlic naan):** $4.00 refunded to your Visa ending 4242 (RF-4000)\n- **#6603 (spring rolls):** $7.00 refunded to your Visa ending 4242 (RF-4001)\n- **#6601 (chicken makhani):** with the incident team under ESC-700, and a specialist will contact you within 24 hours\n\nI'm glad everyone's okay. Have a good evening with your friends!"
  }
